#, no-wrap
msgid "A simulator is a \"perfect world\" version of quantum computing. Here we run the circuit on a simulator for 1000 shots and plot the results. You should see approximately equal counts for the $00$ and $11$ states, with no occurrences of $01$ or $10$, which is the signature of the Bell state's perfect correlation.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang simulator ay isang \"perfect world\" na bersyon ng quantum computing. Dito pinapatakbo natin ang circuit sa isang simulator para sa 1000 shots at iplot ang mga resulta. Dapat mong makita ang halos pantay na counts para sa $00$ at $11$ states, na walang occurrences ng $01$ o $10$, na siyang signature ng perpektong correlation ng Bell state.\n"

